tch is Rs. 750.\n\nThe answer is D"]}, {"Math SolverBNn8": ["Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\nLet the marked price of the watch be x.\n\nWhen the shopkeeper gives a discount of 5%, the selling price becomes 95% of the marked price, which is 0.95x.\n\nWhen the shopkeeper gives a discount of 7%, the selling price becomes 93% of the marked price, which is 0.93x.\n\nIt is given that if he gives a discount of 7%, he earns Rs. 15 less as profit than if he gives a discount of 5%.\n\nLet the profit earned when the discount is 5% be P. Then, the profit earned when the discount is 7% is P - 15.\n\nThe profit is the difference between the marked price and the selling price. So, we can write:\n\nP = x - 0.95x\nP - 15 = x - 0.93x\n\nSimplifying the equations, we get:\n\nP = 0.05x\nP - 15 = 0.07x\n\nNow, we can equate the two expressions for P:\n\n0.05x = 0.07x - 15\n\nSubtracting 0.07x from both sides:\n\n-0.02x = -15\n\nDividing both sides by -0.02:\n\nx = 750\n\nSo, the marked price of the watch is Rs. 750.\n\nThe answer is D"], "Mathematical AnalystTeaX": ["Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\nLet the marked price of the watch be x.\n\nWhen the shopkeeper gives a discount of 5%, the selling price is 95% of the marked price, which is 0.95x.\n\nWhen the shopkeeper gives a discount of 7%, the selling price is 93% of the marked price, which is 0.93x.\n\nThe profit earned by the shopkeeper is the difference between the selling price and the cost price. Let's denote the cost price as c.\n\nWhen the shopkeeper gives a discount of 5%, the profit earned is (0.95x - c).\n\nWhen the shopkeeper gives a discount of 7%, the profit earned is (0.93x - c).\n\nIt is given that when the shopkeeper gives a discount of 7%, he earns Rs. 15 less as profit compared to when he gives a discount of 5%. This can be written as:\n\n(0.95x - c) - (0.93x - c) = 15\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\n\n0.02x = 15\n\nx = 15 / 0.02\n\nx = 750\n\nSo, the marked price of the watch is Rs. 